==Swedish==

===Etymology===
Used by immigrants in [[w:Sweden|Sweden]] in reference to ethnic Swedes. It originates from a [[nickname]] for ''[[Sven]]''.<sup>[citation needed]</sup>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈsvɛ̀nːɛ]|lang=sv}}

===Noun===
{{sv-noun|c}}

# {{label|sv|derogatory|humor|slang}} an ethnic/native [[Swede]] (as opposed to immigrants to Sweden)

====Declension====
{{sv-infl-noun-c-ar|2=svenn}}

====Usage notes====
The word has obtained two different meanings, which sometimes merge. One is referring to [[w:ethnicity|ethnicity]], merely indicating that the individual referred is an [[w:ethnic Swede|ethnic Swede]], and the other indicating that the individual referred is boring, shy and habitually conservative. Because the latter actually is a common viewpoint in Sweden, both different meanings are sometimes used by ethnic Swedes, often ironically.

